      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The history and physical examination allow early identification of the cause of hand pain in most patients. In some cases, however, the etiology of the pain is not obvious and a diagnostic problem arises. The less common causes of hand pain include atypical mycobacterial infection, occult fractures, bone fragments, incomplete carpal coalitions, carpal ligament injuries and several uncommon forms of tendinitis."},
